WEBVTT

00:11.302 --> 00:15.223
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:48.673
I studied Geophysics, but I dropped out.

00:48.757 --> 00:50.341
Once I finished service,

00:50.842 --> 00:53.428
I took the Civil Service Exam
and went to the KMA.

00:54.095 --> 00:55.972
I'm Level Seven, Severe Weather.

00:58.808 --> 00:59.726
Hmm.

01:00.393 --> 01:01.394
[sighs]

01:01.895 --> 01:05.273
Your parents, are they still working?

01:09.110 --> 01:15.825
We did a CT scan and there's a mass
of about 3 centimeters on his right lung.

01:15.909 --> 01:17.327
We should investigate.

01:17.410 --> 01:20.246
Going forward,
I'd highly recommend a biopsy.

01:20.330 --> 01:22.332
[somber music]

01:26.086 --> 01:29.005
My mother isn't with us.
She died years ago.

01:31.341 --> 01:32.425
My dad…

01:35.595 --> 01:36.763
[breathes deeply]

01:37.555 --> 01:41.142
…was a construction worker
till he got hurt.

01:42.477 --> 01:44.103
He can't work 'cause of that.

01:50.819 --> 01:52.028
Oh, oh…

01:54.239 --> 01:55.490
[Mrs. Bae] I see.

01:58.576 --> 01:59.828
[sighs deeply]

02:05.792 --> 02:07.627
[Si-woo] The rain said to the wind…

02:08.586 --> 02:11.047
BIOPSY CONSENT FORM

02:11.131 --> 02:13.341
[nurse] He'll need to stay
at the hospital for a day,

02:13.424 --> 02:15.093
maybe two for the biopsy.

02:15.677 --> 02:18.221
Also, we need
a guardian signature right there.

02:20.682 --> 02:22.684
PATIENT OR GUARDIAN SIGNATURE

02:29.315 --> 02:31.818
[snoring]

02:34.821 --> 02:37.782
[Si-woo] …"You roar. And I'll fall."

02:41.536 --> 02:42.495
[sighs]

02:43.663 --> 02:45.957
[somber music continues]

02:49.085 --> 02:54.716
EPISODE 15
ENSEMBLE

02:58.636 --> 02:59.846
[Ha-kyung] Where are you going?

02:59.929 --> 03:00.930
Oh…

03:02.223 --> 03:03.850
Oh, you're still here?

03:05.768 --> 03:08.354
You're not supposed
to be walking around. Don't leave.

03:08.438 --> 03:12.317
Ah, these insurance assholes
are so intense now.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.986
They're acting
like I'm some insurance scam

03:15.069 --> 03:17.030
wherein they said the cops are watching.

03:17.113 --> 03:18.364
They don't believe you?

03:19.032 --> 03:21.492
Seriously, I was just crossing the road,

03:21.576 --> 03:24.287
and then this car
was going so fast that it hit me.

03:24.370 --> 03:26.873
[Myung-han sighs]

03:27.999 --> 03:28.833
Wait a sec.

03:30.335 --> 03:32.503
Si-woo didn't come with you, huh?

03:32.587 --> 03:35.340
There wasn't any time for me
to call him. I'll call him now.

03:35.423 --> 03:38.217
[sighs]
Nah. Bothering him is not worth it.

03:38.301 --> 03:41.679
Swear I'll send you the money
for the hospital bill and all that.

03:42.263 --> 03:45.850
So you don't have
to nag Si-woo about it. Deal?

03:48.061 --> 03:51.189
The doctor said
they need to do more tests.

03:51.272 --> 03:52.398
[sighs]

03:53.483 --> 03:55.151
You're more gullible than I thought.

03:56.069 --> 03:59.280
A hospital is just trying to get
as much out of you as they can.

03:59.364 --> 04:00.365
You know what I'm saying?

04:00.949 --> 04:03.284
It's on the CAT scan.
Something's on your lung.

04:03.368 --> 04:05.078
That happens to everyone.

04:05.161 --> 04:08.581
When you get old, you get lumps
and stuff. It's natural.

04:13.211 --> 04:14.671
Were you already aware of it?

04:17.840 --> 04:22.595
Hey, lady, if you got any money,
you know, 10 thou,

04:22.679 --> 04:25.306
would you spot me, so I can get a bite?

04:30.353 --> 04:31.688
They wanna do a biopsy.

04:31.771 --> 04:34.649
I gave them your information.
You'd stay here a day or two.

04:37.277 --> 04:38.903
[Ha-kyung] I strongly recommend doing it.

04:39.654 --> 04:41.114
But it's really up to you.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.491
Si-woo doesn't need to know, okay?

04:46.202 --> 04:47.787
It's our secret.

04:53.918 --> 04:55.378
- [switch clicks]
- [groans]

04:55.461 --> 04:56.838
Turn it off.

04:57.463 --> 04:59.382
Oh, I'm sorry.

05:06.556 --> 05:07.557
[door lock clicks]

05:17.066 --> 05:20.278
[breathes deeply]

05:23.448 --> 05:24.449
[switch clicks]

05:24.532 --> 05:25.742
Mom, you're here.

05:27.910 --> 05:29.579
[inhales]

05:29.662 --> 05:31.205
I had some thinking to do.

05:31.956 --> 05:33.624
Why? You can't think at your own house?

05:34.876 --> 05:36.210
I guess not.

05:36.794 --> 05:40.798
Oh, I saw Lee Si-woo
and we had a little talk.

05:42.508 --> 05:43.968
Mom, why was Lee Si-woo here?

05:44.469 --> 05:45.678
What do you mean "little talk"?

05:47.764 --> 05:49.140
Why is it so important, huh?

05:49.223 --> 05:50.975
If you're not dating anymore.

05:52.727 --> 05:53.936
We aren't, but…

05:54.645 --> 05:55.730
[sighs]

05:55.813 --> 05:57.231
It's good that you did.

05:57.315 --> 05:59.734
There's no need for every boyfriend
to be a husband.

06:00.401 --> 06:01.694
You should get some rest.

06:13.706 --> 06:16.751
- [door closes]
- [door lock beeps]

06:17.585 --> 06:18.920
[sighs]

06:26.677 --> 06:28.679
[gentle music]

06:30.056 --> 06:31.224
[beeps]

06:35.520 --> 06:37.814
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

06:44.779 --> 06:45.822
[sighs]

06:45.905 --> 06:47.323
Door is closing.

06:51.119 --> 06:54.330
["Love Hurts a Little More"
by Kim Na Young]

07:07.635 --> 07:08.928
[sighs]

07:19.272 --> 07:20.565
[heavy sigh]

07:38.458 --> 07:40.501
[reporter] The first cold wave
of the season is persisting,

07:40.585 --> 07:43.629
and Seoul saw its first frost of the year.

07:43.713 --> 07:47.717
The temperature is continuing to drop,
while Seoul is currently three degrees.

07:47.800 --> 07:51.137
The low today is 0.7 degrees in the city.

07:51.220 --> 07:54.765
The KMA forecast predicts
chilly temperatures this evening

07:54.849 --> 07:57.351
with things warming up closer
to average temperatures

07:57.435 --> 07:59.353
for the season by tomorrow afternoon.

07:59.437 --> 08:02.773
However, the midlands
will be trading the cold weather

08:02.857 --> 08:04.484
for strong winds.

08:04.567 --> 08:07.612
We recommend taking precautions
against those high winds.

08:07.695 --> 08:10.865
The air today is fairly clear.
The daily average for the fine dust level

08:10.948 --> 08:13.910
is in the good to normal range
for the entire country.

08:13.993 --> 08:17.079
Far from shore, and the skies
to the central Southeast--

08:20.958 --> 08:24.378
You don't have to come in.
I can see the doctor alone.

08:28.799 --> 08:30.343
Why aren't you saying anything?

08:31.552 --> 08:33.304
I'm thinking about what you said.

08:35.056 --> 08:37.016
Can I have a little while
to think about it?

08:38.184 --> 08:41.562
If we wait too long,
then they can't do anything for me.

08:42.813 --> 08:45.733
[emotional music]

08:45.816 --> 08:47.693
[breathes deeply]

08:47.777 --> 08:50.571
Every time I try to think it through,
we just can't afford it.

08:52.281 --> 08:54.075
Having a kid is costly.

08:54.700 --> 08:57.203
The doctor visits, delivery, the recovery.

08:57.286 --> 08:59.080
We can move somewhere cheaper,

09:00.081 --> 09:02.333
then we could scrape together enough
for the birth cost.

09:02.416 --> 09:03.960
After that, I don't know.

09:09.507 --> 09:11.592
It doesn't get cheaper
once the baby's here.

09:12.176 --> 09:15.596
I'd use up my maternity leave
and we'd need to get a nanny.

09:15.680 --> 09:19.725
I looked into it, and they cost
as much as my starting salary.

09:22.979 --> 09:26.482
There's kindergarten
or there's something like that.

09:26.566 --> 09:27.400
[sighs]

09:27.483 --> 09:30.236
There's a while
when the kid's too young for daycare.

09:34.448 --> 09:36.450
Oppa, you go to work
when the sun comes up.

09:36.534 --> 09:38.035
And I stay late almost every day.

09:38.619 --> 09:41.914
There's parental leave.
And you could take extra time off.

09:44.667 --> 09:45.918
I couldn't go back.

09:46.002 --> 09:49.005
[Yu-jin] I just got my own column.
They're giving me a chance.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.048
I don't want to give up this opportunity.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.925
And I don't want to give up
my career either.

09:53.009 --> 09:55.845
[pensive music]

09:58.598 --> 10:00.016
[sighs]

10:00.099 --> 10:02.476
We got married really impulsively.

10:03.686 --> 10:06.647
And we really can't bring a child
into the world like that.

10:12.445 --> 10:13.571
[car honks]

10:17.992 --> 10:20.369
[engine revs]

10:26.584 --> 10:27.835
[phone vibrates]

10:30.713 --> 10:32.340
Hello? What do you need?

10:32.423 --> 10:34.050
Hey.
[inhales]

10:34.133 --> 10:36.552
They say they might do it this afternoon.

10:36.636 --> 10:39.513
They're doing a blood test
and some other things.

10:41.557 --> 10:42.600
Oh, all right.

10:43.267 --> 10:44.935
They said I can't eat after ten.

10:45.770 --> 10:47.772
[sighs]
I should have had more food.

10:47.855 --> 10:50.024
I had breakfast,
but I would have eaten more.

10:50.107 --> 10:51.984
[Myung-han] Jeez, I'm hungry.

10:52.068 --> 10:55.154
I'm heading into work right now,
and I'll be in a meeting right after.

10:55.946 --> 10:57.031
Oh, hey.

10:58.199 --> 11:01.243
Si-woo doesn't… know yet, does he?

11:02.453 --> 11:03.788
I have to go. Goodbye.

11:04.872 --> 11:05.831
[call ends]

11:07.667 --> 11:08.709
[sighs]

11:12.797 --> 11:14.507
[yawns]

11:14.590 --> 11:17.635
Huh? Why are you here?

11:17.718 --> 11:19.428
- You slept here?
- Oh!

11:19.512 --> 11:22.014
Uh, no, it's not that. No.

11:22.098 --> 11:23.766
Your apartment search failed?

11:26.143 --> 11:28.312
Don't tell, um, the Director, please.

11:28.396 --> 11:30.815
Why? You two had a fight?

11:30.898 --> 11:33.526
[chuckles]
No. I don't want her to worry.

11:34.360 --> 11:35.569
You're too sweet, you know.

11:35.653 --> 11:37.780
- [chuckles]
- Go on, get.

11:39.532 --> 11:41.033
[laughs]

11:42.368 --> 11:43.577
[sighs]

11:45.037 --> 11:47.206
- Good morning, everyone.
- [Young-gil] Hmm.

11:47.289 --> 11:49.583
- Working hard?
- You're here early.

11:49.667 --> 11:52.878
Ooh, today looks like
it's a lot colder than we forecast.

11:52.962 --> 11:54.046
Nah, it'll be fine.

11:54.130 --> 11:58.050
[Young-gil] The continental anticyclone
in Siberia has momentarily strengthened.

11:58.134 --> 12:00.010
But there's a strong warm current
in the south,

12:00.094 --> 12:01.470
so tomorrow, it will be warm again.

12:01.554 --> 12:03.556
And our ensemble forecast then?

12:03.639 --> 12:06.434
Ms. Lee, would you give me
the ensemble we printed earlier?

12:06.517 --> 12:08.602
ENSEMBLE FORECASTING: A METHOD
THAT MINIMIZES ERRORS AND UNCERTAINTIES

12:08.686 --> 12:10.312
BY USING SEVERAL NUMERICAL MODELS
TO MAKE VARIOUS PREDICTIONS

12:10.396 --> 12:12.064
- Here.
- Here you are.

12:12.898 --> 12:16.318
The NWP model and the ensemble prediction

12:16.402 --> 12:18.904
all show temperatures
rising tomorrow afternoon.

12:18.988 --> 12:19.989
So I see.

12:20.072 --> 12:23.284
We shouldn't have to change that much
from what we sent out yesterday.

12:24.285 --> 12:26.871
Well, looks like an easy one,
all thanks to you.

12:26.954 --> 12:28.539
You got a great Team One, Director.

12:28.622 --> 12:29.623
[chuckles]

12:31.876 --> 12:33.794
[light music]

12:35.629 --> 12:36.922
[Si-woo] Good morning.

12:37.006 --> 12:38.340
- [Soo-jin] Hello.
- [Myung-ju] Hi.

12:38.424 --> 12:39.925
[Ha-kyung] Good morning. Oh, right.

12:41.385 --> 12:43.137
You left this at my apartment yesterday.

12:43.846 --> 12:44.930
[Si-woo] Ah…

12:46.474 --> 12:47.641
Right.

12:48.517 --> 12:50.311
I guess I was sort of scattered.

12:50.394 --> 12:53.063
My mother often does that
to people that she sees.

12:55.608 --> 12:57.067
[whispers]
Oh, that's very nice.

12:58.903 --> 13:01.614
[playful music]

13:04.074 --> 13:05.367
Let's talk later.

13:07.703 --> 13:09.038
Oh, yeah.

13:15.878 --> 13:17.838
[Soo-jin] He's already meeting her mom?

13:18.506 --> 13:20.841
[Myung-ju] Oh, wow.
It's going really well.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.344
[Seok-ho] Don't get ahead of yourselves.

13:23.427 --> 13:25.846
[Myung-ju] Stop being so sour.
They're great.

13:25.930 --> 13:28.057
[phone vibrates]

13:30.392 --> 13:32.228
[mouse clicking]

13:36.524 --> 13:37.650
Yes?

13:37.733 --> 13:39.068
I'm not supposed to…

13:39.735 --> 13:41.820
have water on my fast, right?

13:41.904 --> 13:44.615
I'm at work and I can't talk.
I'm so sorry.

13:46.075 --> 13:47.117
[call ends]

13:52.081 --> 13:53.749
[exhales]

13:59.129 --> 14:01.757
[somber music]

14:08.847 --> 14:09.890
You want a coffee?

14:13.018 --> 14:14.103
Oh, sure.

14:17.773 --> 14:19.400
[machine clicks, beeps]

14:33.122 --> 14:34.331
[Ha-kyung] Hey, uh…

14:34.957 --> 14:37.877
Have you called and talked
to your father recently?

14:40.337 --> 14:41.171
Why?

14:41.922 --> 14:43.382
[machine beeps]

14:43.465 --> 14:46.844
It's just it's starting
to get a bit colder, so I…

14:46.927 --> 14:49.054
I told you. We don't chitchat like that.

14:53.517 --> 14:56.395
It's not too hard just to call
and check on him, though, right?

14:56.478 --> 14:57.938
It's not that it's hard.

14:58.439 --> 14:59.732
I don't want to.

15:02.651 --> 15:05.696
Still, your father's getting older.
It wouldn't be the worst for you to try.

15:06.947 --> 15:09.199
Not all dads in this world
are someone you talk to.

15:09.283 --> 15:11.452
In his whole life, he's never cared

15:11.535 --> 15:14.330
how I was doing
or whether I was feeling all right.

15:14.413 --> 15:16.540
And I don't see why
I shouldn't act like that too.

15:16.624 --> 15:18.667
You think we should call just to talk?

15:18.751 --> 15:20.502
I don't think he wants us to.

15:20.586 --> 15:22.504
Regardless of how the weather goes.

15:25.215 --> 15:26.091
[sighs]

15:26.926 --> 15:28.427
You'll regret this.

15:30.804 --> 15:33.766
If you ignore him now
out of some sort of anger,

15:34.642 --> 15:37.978
you could regret it down the road, still.

15:41.857 --> 15:45.319
And you can never go back
no matter how much it hurts.

15:45.402 --> 15:46.236
I won't.

15:47.112 --> 15:49.073
I won't ever regret it. I swear.

15:50.115 --> 15:53.410
There's no moment
I want to redo, not with…

15:54.828 --> 15:56.163
Not with him.

16:10.928 --> 16:14.014
We had a disagreement over his father.

16:14.098 --> 16:15.474
[machine clicks]

16:15.557 --> 16:17.017
I don't need to know that.

16:19.353 --> 16:21.063
No, you don't.
[awkward chuckle]

16:23.565 --> 16:26.318
PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:28.862 --> 16:31.490
LOOKING FOR A PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:31.573 --> 16:33.158
HIRING FULL-TIME HOUSEKEEPERS

16:36.245 --> 16:40.249
DIAPER COSTS PER MONTH

16:40.332 --> 16:43.002
[mouse scrolling]

16:48.632 --> 16:51.301
BABY FORMULA COST PER MONTH

16:59.059 --> 17:00.102
[mouse clicks]

17:05.482 --> 17:08.110
[sweet music]

17:16.660 --> 17:18.412
- [Min-jun] Sir.
- Yeah?

17:19.788 --> 17:21.290
Aren't you gonna eat?

17:21.874 --> 17:25.335
Oh. I'm not… really hungry.

17:25.419 --> 17:27.296
- You please go on.
- Okay, well, um…

17:27.379 --> 17:28.505
[Ki-jun] Yeah.

17:29.339 --> 17:31.967
Sir, are you gonna eat?

17:32.801 --> 17:34.470
Oh, it's time already?

17:35.137 --> 17:37.848
[grunts]
Really? Okay. Let's eat. Let's eat.

17:38.432 --> 17:41.393
- Come on. Let's all go, huh? Let's all go.
- I'll go, then.

17:41.477 --> 17:44.855
I… I'm really not hungry.
Seriously. You can go.

17:44.938 --> 17:46.356
- Suit yourself.
- [Ki-jun] Yeah.

17:46.440 --> 17:47.483
[Ju-won] Let's go eat.

17:48.442 --> 17:49.985
What should we get today?

17:51.612 --> 17:53.155
Ah, let's go.

17:54.615 --> 17:55.783
[door closes]

17:59.745 --> 18:02.247
[gentle music]

18:02.331 --> 18:04.166
PARENTING COMMUNITY

18:08.212 --> 18:09.671
JOIN COMMUNITY

18:09.755 --> 18:11.548
SUBMIT INFORMATION TO JOIN COMMUNITY

18:11.632 --> 18:14.885
BABY BUMP NICKNAME

18:19.515 --> 18:22.476
[keyboard clacking]

18:24.061 --> 18:25.145
Yeah, yeah.

18:25.229 --> 18:28.357
So, uh, you talked to Bo-mi yet?

18:28.440 --> 18:30.692
Yes. However, um…

18:30.776 --> 18:32.111
What does she want?

18:32.194 --> 18:34.363
- She wants to go eat.
- Wait, huh?

18:34.905 --> 18:36.990
Not some new clothes or some sort of--

18:37.074 --> 18:39.493
No. I was told she doesn't want clothes.

18:39.576 --> 18:41.703
All she want is a meal with her ma and pa.

18:41.787 --> 18:43.831
I can't remember the last time

18:43.914 --> 18:45.999
the three of us
went out to eat altogether.

18:46.083 --> 18:47.251
I'm sure she can't either.

18:47.835 --> 18:50.337
[Hyang-rae] When was it?
When she was five or six?

18:50.420 --> 18:51.755
Uh…

18:51.839 --> 18:55.384
I know we went
to that family restaurant then.

18:55.467 --> 18:58.053
Of course, we had
that big argument on the way home.

18:58.720 --> 19:01.431
Oh, right. Right. Mm.

19:01.515 --> 19:05.060
Okay. I'll call her tutor
and cancel her private session today,

19:05.144 --> 19:06.353
so get a reservation.

19:06.436 --> 19:07.896
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

19:07.980 --> 19:10.274
Tell me where,
and I'll take Bo-mi there, okay?

19:10.858 --> 19:12.526
Also, Bo-mi likes pasta.

19:12.609 --> 19:13.652
Pasta.

19:14.153 --> 19:15.571
Yeah. Thank you.

19:20.450 --> 19:24.663
[sighs]
Um Dong-han. What were you thinking?

19:24.746 --> 19:28.417
[breathes deeply]
Even way back then, you were always…

19:29.251 --> 19:30.752
- an ass.
- [Seok-ho] Mr. Um.

19:30.836 --> 19:33.463
I printed out the data on the ECMWF.

19:33.547 --> 19:35.215
It's on your desk to review.

19:35.299 --> 19:36.633
I'll also have the KIM for you.

19:36.717 --> 19:38.343
Okay, all right.

19:42.306 --> 19:43.765
[exhales deeply]

19:43.849 --> 19:45.058
[tongue clicks]

19:46.935 --> 19:49.271
- Here's the citrus tea you ordered.
- Oh, thanks so much.

19:49.354 --> 19:50.898
A citrus tea also. Thank you.

19:51.481 --> 19:53.483
- Oh, Mr. Kim.
- [chuckles]

19:54.109 --> 19:55.611
Ah, hmm, yeah.
[sniffles]

19:55.694 --> 19:57.196
It's cold, huh?

19:57.279 --> 20:00.240
It got so cold around here. It happened
in such a short time, you know.

20:00.324 --> 20:03.076
Yeah. There's no middle ground
in this country.

20:03.160 --> 20:04.328
Right.

20:04.411 --> 20:07.331
Oh, how is your…
your new recruit coming along?

20:07.915 --> 20:08.957
Hmm?

20:09.791 --> 20:11.543
[sighs]

20:11.627 --> 20:14.129
I don't know what to say to you
to make you understand,

20:14.213 --> 20:17.466
but it's necessary to always do this
with the high-res reports.

20:18.050 --> 20:20.886
You told me to look
at the forecast field report, sir,

20:20.969 --> 20:21.929
not those.

20:23.639 --> 20:24.514
[sighs]

20:26.600 --> 20:29.436
You've been here long enough.
You should know how to perform your role.

20:31.021 --> 20:33.273
- I'm sorry.
- Redo it all.

20:34.399 --> 20:35.525
- Okay.
- [mouse clicks]

20:40.239 --> 20:42.991
What? What is it? Do you want some help?

20:43.075 --> 20:44.868
[chuckles]
Oh, no.

20:48.413 --> 20:50.040
[sighs]

20:50.123 --> 20:52.167
- [keyboard clacks]
- [mouse clicks]

20:52.251 --> 20:55.587
I heard that the Policy Division's
been searching for a way to poach her.

20:57.089 --> 20:58.048
You didn't know?

21:01.885 --> 21:03.011
[exhales]

21:03.095 --> 21:06.056
It's hard, right?
Here, drink that. Citrus tea.

21:06.640 --> 21:08.517
Oh, thank you.

21:14.648 --> 21:16.024
- [sighs]
- [mouse clicks]

21:19.778 --> 21:20.862
[chuckles]

21:31.498 --> 21:32.457
Director.

21:32.958 --> 21:36.295
The air pressure flow
looks kinda odd, huh?

21:36.378 --> 21:37.337
Where?

21:37.421 --> 21:40.382
Here. The way the jet stream
isn't weakening,

21:40.465 --> 21:44.011
I don't think the upper COL
is headed eastwards at all now.

21:44.636 --> 21:46.763
[tense music]

21:48.348 --> 21:52.519
The NWP model has the temperature
going back up tomorrow afternoon.

21:52.602 --> 21:55.272
Yeah, that's that, but Si-woo, come here.

21:55.355 --> 21:56.189
[Si-woo] Okay.

22:01.987 --> 22:03.864
Here. What do you think of this?

22:05.365 --> 22:06.408
Hmm.

22:08.535 --> 22:10.787
I think we should compare it
to the real condition data

22:10.871 --> 22:13.248
and analyze the possible outcomes
for this pattern.

22:13.332 --> 22:14.583
Yeah. Something's not right.

22:14.666 --> 22:16.585
- Yeah.
- What is it? I…

22:16.668 --> 22:19.588
If you look here, the jet stream's
expansion is too stable.

22:19.671 --> 22:22.049
There's not really a record
of this sort of behavior, right?

22:22.132 --> 22:24.134
Yeah. That's what I find strange too.

22:27.971 --> 22:30.140
[Dong-han] Let's look
at the ensemble prediction,

22:30.223 --> 22:32.476
and perform an analysis on the scenarios

22:32.559 --> 22:35.228
that suggest a cold wave
could carry on for a while.

22:35.312 --> 22:37.189
Okay. On our meeting, I'm gonna

22:37.272 --> 22:39.649
go of the current NWP,
if that's all right.

22:39.733 --> 22:40.609
Mm-hmm.

22:41.568 --> 22:44.905
Mr. Shin. Send me time series data
for the major regions.

22:44.988 --> 22:45.989
Okay.

22:49.993 --> 22:51.119
[mouse clicks]

22:51.203 --> 22:53.246
- Okay, I sent it.
- Mm, okay.

22:59.336 --> 23:00.420
[sighs]

23:04.341 --> 23:05.467
[message alert tone]

23:12.724 --> 23:14.142
[Seok-ho] How's work going?

23:15.435 --> 23:18.522
[Tae-kyung sighs heavily]
Not great.

23:20.148 --> 23:21.358
[Seok-ho] How come?

23:26.154 --> 23:28.365
[playful music]

23:30.242 --> 23:32.285
[Tae-kyung] The weather's too nice.

23:35.497 --> 23:37.707
[sighs, clicks tongue]

23:37.791 --> 23:40.335
Last time, she said the sky
was too cloudy to work.

23:41.837 --> 23:43.755
She doesn't wanna work
when it's cold either.

23:45.090 --> 23:46.883
[Seok-ho] Is there anything
I can do to help?

23:50.887 --> 23:52.055
[giggles]

24:03.441 --> 24:04.943
Ma, I'll be out for a little.

24:11.158 --> 24:12.868
Whoa, it's cold.

24:12.951 --> 24:15.829
Oh, Mom, you should have told me
it was so cold.

24:16.746 --> 24:18.331
Where's my fluffy coat?

24:18.415 --> 24:20.167
Mom! My fluffy coat?

24:28.175 --> 24:32.220
I really have to find a coat
at my age for my 40-year-old daughter?

24:32.304 --> 24:33.930
Ma, what's wrong?

24:34.014 --> 24:35.056
You're upset?

24:35.140 --> 24:37.350
I don't even have the energy to be upset.

24:37.434 --> 24:39.561
The both of you are on your own now.

24:39.644 --> 24:41.605
Find the coat and get it yourself.

24:41.688 --> 24:44.900
[Mrs. Bae] I don't care.
[grunts]

24:48.028 --> 24:49.070
[door slams]

24:52.324 --> 24:55.118
[man] As predicted,
the cold core is moving south

24:55.202 --> 24:57.454
as the continental anticyclone develops

24:57.537 --> 25:00.457
and national temperatures
are expected to drop 10 to 15 degrees.

25:00.540 --> 25:01.875
[Bong-chan] Mm, I see.

25:01.958 --> 25:04.419
So then, when do we expect it to end?

25:05.253 --> 25:08.340
According to the NWP
and ensemble prediction modeling,

25:08.423 --> 25:10.175
there's a strong chance
of warmer temperatures

25:10.258 --> 25:11.843
returning tomorrow, however…

25:13.470 --> 25:15.305
Okay, so? However what?

25:17.349 --> 25:20.227
Uh, however,
we're investigating an anomaly

25:20.310 --> 25:21.937
that was found in the ensemble prediction.

25:22.646 --> 25:24.439
- [glasses clack]
- And what?

25:25.899 --> 25:27.275
[Bong-chan] Pull it up.

25:28.860 --> 25:30.028
ENSEMBLE PREDICTION

25:30.111 --> 25:33.198
[Dong-han] Of the 32 models
in the ensemble prediction,

25:33.281 --> 25:35.909
there are four showing
three more days of severe cold.

25:36.701 --> 25:38.578
And the whole point
of the ensemble prediction

25:38.662 --> 25:40.330
is to see the outcome
that's more supported.

25:40.413 --> 25:41.665
[Si-woo] That's true.

25:41.748 --> 25:43.583
But in this case,
things are a little different.

25:44.209 --> 25:46.253
[keyboard clacks]

25:49.214 --> 25:51.800
The biggest thing
is a jet stream 10km high

25:51.883 --> 25:53.843
that isn't losing any strength right now.

25:53.927 --> 25:57.097
- [monitor trills]
- And the strong COL at 5km

25:57.180 --> 25:59.224
doesn't look much more likely
to head east.

26:00.642 --> 26:02.686
What? So 4 of 32 models
were like that one?

26:02.769 --> 26:04.854
They're showing a delay
of three to four more days.

26:05.522 --> 26:06.648
Yes.

26:08.108 --> 26:09.150
So now what?

26:09.734 --> 26:10.944
As things are currently--

26:11.027 --> 26:13.822
We may have to retract our forecast.

26:13.905 --> 26:16.199
[tense music]

26:27.127 --> 26:28.545
[blows air]

26:29.587 --> 26:30.755
[exhales]

26:31.881 --> 26:33.216
[Ki-jun] Forecaster Lee Si-woo.

26:33.800 --> 26:36.136
Do you know what it means for us
to retract a forecast?

26:37.429 --> 26:38.471
Yeah, I'm aware.

26:40.640 --> 26:43.059
[tense music intensifying]

26:44.686 --> 26:46.354
And you agree, then?

26:49.024 --> 26:50.275
Retract the forecast?

26:50.358 --> 26:53.194
- No, we can't.
- If we're wrong, it's hell.

26:59.117 --> 27:02.579
[suspenseful music]

27:03.872 --> 27:05.040
[Bong-chan] Director Jin?

27:06.541 --> 27:07.792
You want to retract it too?

27:09.669 --> 27:10.920
Yes, I'm in favor.

27:11.755 --> 27:14.674
[tapping, sighs deeply]

27:20.555 --> 27:23.433
[tense music]

27:25.685 --> 27:27.812
[phone vibrates]

27:30.106 --> 27:32.275
Yes, Mr. Lee. I'm almost at the office.

27:32.359 --> 27:34.319
[Lee] No! No, no, no, no! Stop, stop!

27:34.402 --> 27:36.863
Turn back around
and go straight to the KMA.

27:36.946 --> 27:40.575
What for? I already sent you
the articles for tomorrow.

27:40.658 --> 27:42.952
[sighs]
The KMA is…

27:44.037 --> 27:45.372
They're retracting their forecast.

27:45.455 --> 27:46.581
What?

27:49.584 --> 27:51.086
What are you going to do?

27:51.628 --> 27:53.129
You'll get backlash if you reverse it,

27:53.213 --> 27:57.342
so you could get the director
of Team One at your throat.

27:57.425 --> 28:00.428
I can't ignore the data
out of fear of others' opinions.

28:00.512 --> 28:03.515
Doesn't the group report show
we could stick with the current forecast?

28:03.598 --> 28:06.351
Well, Mr. Um and Lee Si-woo…

28:07.060 --> 28:08.561
and myself all agree here.

28:09.270 --> 28:12.440
So you're willing to take
all the blame for Lee Si-woo's theory?

28:12.524 --> 28:13.400
[inhales deeply]

28:13.483 --> 28:17.445
You know, I made all these mistakes
when I was younger

28:17.529 --> 28:18.571
and didn't know better.

28:18.655 --> 28:21.324
And my director would cover
for his forecasters.

28:23.201 --> 28:25.412
That's how I got to where I am now.

28:25.995 --> 28:29.040
I'd like to do the same for them now.

28:31.376 --> 28:33.628
Now it's our turn. Now that we're older.

28:37.632 --> 28:39.175
[deep inhale]

28:39.259 --> 28:42.095
[sighs]
Well, I envy you.

28:43.054 --> 28:47.475
You act, and talk, and behave
like you're really a responsible adult.

28:50.228 --> 28:51.396
Is that sarcasm?

28:51.980 --> 28:54.691
No, seriously. I really mean it.

28:54.774 --> 28:56.317
What's with you all of a sudden?

28:58.069 --> 29:01.489
[sighs]
Recently, I've been feeling like…

29:02.449 --> 29:03.491
You know how they say,

29:03.575 --> 29:06.119
"Nothing's really free in life
and all has a cost"?

29:06.202 --> 29:09.205
And I… have been feeling
so much of that weight,

29:09.289 --> 29:11.166
so much need to be responsible.

29:11.791 --> 29:13.543
And that it's really hard…

29:14.502 --> 29:16.004
to be an adult.

29:19.924 --> 29:20.925
[inhales deeply]

29:21.009 --> 29:25.138
Okay, so if the Chief Team wants
to retract the forecast, we'll retract it.

29:25.221 --> 29:27.390
We'll take care
of whatever comes out of this.

29:30.310 --> 29:31.978
Okay, well, I'll go send it, Director.

29:32.061 --> 29:33.438
Okay.

29:33.521 --> 29:34.606
Yeah, sure.

29:37.150 --> 29:40.195
[calm music]

29:41.654 --> 29:43.281
[phone vibrates]

29:44.324 --> 29:47.118
SI-WOO'S FATHER

29:47.994 --> 29:49.412
[keys jingle]

29:52.540 --> 29:54.375
[sighs]
Yes, what is it now?

29:55.376 --> 29:57.504
Uh, well, they told me, uh…

29:57.587 --> 30:00.089
They say that I have
to go for my biopsy, so…

30:00.715 --> 30:01.966
Oh, okay.

30:03.051 --> 30:04.302
Well, anyway…

30:04.385 --> 30:05.929
[inhales deeply]

30:06.012 --> 30:08.139
…thank you for the hospital room.

30:08.765 --> 30:11.142
[Myung-han] I'm living high,
thanks to my son.

30:11.226 --> 30:15.146
I'll put in a good word for you
with Si-woo sometime.

30:15.772 --> 30:16.606
To be honest,

30:17.106 --> 30:19.567
you're not my type, Director.
You're a little high-strung.

30:20.735 --> 30:24.948
But Si-woo's got a better eye
for, uh, for girls than I do, huh?

30:25.031 --> 30:26.908
[Myung-han laughs]
Right?

30:26.991 --> 30:28.326
Uh, actually…

30:29.369 --> 30:30.745
we're not together now.

30:33.832 --> 30:34.791
Not together?

30:35.416 --> 30:36.584
Wait, why not?

30:37.669 --> 30:39.170
Hey, did he do something?

30:39.254 --> 30:40.588
Uh, no.

30:40.672 --> 30:41.840
Well, then why?

30:42.799 --> 30:44.467
Wait, did he get aggressive?

30:45.051 --> 30:46.052
No.

30:46.803 --> 30:49.222
[sucks teeth]
That's strange.

30:49.848 --> 30:53.351
He's not the type to stray
or get drunk and make a scene.

30:54.102 --> 30:55.061
Oh, no. Did he?

30:55.937 --> 30:57.188
It wasn't that, sir.

30:57.272 --> 30:58.898
Then why didn't it work?

30:59.774 --> 31:02.235
Why have you been so nice

31:02.318 --> 31:03.236
if you broke up?

31:03.319 --> 31:05.238
Why did you get me that test

31:05.321 --> 31:06.990
and make sure I had a room?

31:07.615 --> 31:11.369
Si-woo's still a part
of our forecasting department here, sir.

31:11.953 --> 31:14.080
[Ha-kyung] As his senior
at work and his director,

31:14.163 --> 31:16.583
it's prudent that I take care
of this for him.

31:16.666 --> 31:19.252
[sighs, tongue clicks]

31:19.335 --> 31:22.297
Then I guess you're still hung up
on Si-woo, huh, no?

31:25.091 --> 31:26.551
I gotta take care of something now.

31:26.634 --> 31:28.678
I hope everything goes well
with your biopsy.

31:33.141 --> 31:34.267
[tongue clicks]

31:34.350 --> 31:36.436
[sighs]
What an idiot.

31:37.729 --> 31:39.731
You hold on to a woman like that.

31:42.859 --> 31:44.110
[sighs]

31:57.790 --> 31:59.208
[groans]

32:08.384 --> 32:09.469
Ms. Chae!

32:10.053 --> 32:12.555
What are you doing here? Are you sick?

32:13.222 --> 32:15.266
[groans]
It's my stomach.

32:16.517 --> 32:17.477
Are you in pain?

32:18.311 --> 32:19.312
Huh?

32:20.313 --> 32:21.397
[sighs]

32:25.026 --> 32:26.110
You're a little clogged up.

32:27.070 --> 32:29.197
[Eun-ji] I'm telling you
stress messes with your gut.

32:32.325 --> 32:34.202
Try this. It's herbal medicine.

32:34.285 --> 32:36.120
You wait an hour, you'll feel better.

32:37.830 --> 32:39.540
Don't let yourself suffer.

32:39.624 --> 32:41.960
When life gets hard,
take some medicine, okay?

32:43.211 --> 32:44.253
Mm-hmm.

32:44.337 --> 32:45.463
I'm going in now.

32:46.547 --> 32:47.382
You come in too.

32:49.509 --> 32:50.885
[sighs]

32:51.719 --> 32:53.513
[phone vibrates]

32:57.642 --> 33:00.561
AREUM OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY
YOUR RESERVATION HAS BEEN CONFIRMED

33:03.564 --> 33:05.566
[somber music]

33:12.949 --> 33:16.744
We'll give you a short overview
of the changes first,

33:16.828 --> 33:18.454
then we will take questions, okay?

33:24.794 --> 33:28.131
Our data now shows the drop
in temperature is remaining strong

33:28.214 --> 33:30.341
throughout the next three or four days.

33:30.425 --> 33:32.093
The cold wave, which the forecast

33:32.176 --> 33:34.303
previously had subsiding
tomorrow afternoon

33:34.387 --> 33:37.265
is now expected to last until this weekend

33:37.348 --> 33:40.184
around Korea's center
and the southern inland regions.

33:40.268 --> 33:41.561
- Okay. Bye.
- Okay.

33:41.644 --> 33:42.812
- Okay.
- Bye.

33:44.272 --> 33:46.232
- Okay. Bye.
- Bye.

33:47.442 --> 33:48.985
[door slides open]

33:51.863 --> 33:53.239
[door slides close]

34:00.830 --> 34:01.748
Aren't you going home?

34:02.248 --> 34:04.042
You go on. I'm gonna review this.

34:15.261 --> 34:17.680
[door slides open]

34:23.936 --> 34:25.354
[sighs]

34:32.695 --> 34:34.322
[sighs]

34:47.168 --> 34:50.171
[beeps, hums]

34:52.048 --> 34:53.174
Thank you.

34:56.511 --> 34:58.471
The jet stream will stay, right?

34:58.554 --> 35:02.308
Only the jet stream knows
what the jet stream's gonna do.

35:02.391 --> 35:04.227
[Si-woo] The forecast is already out.

35:04.310 --> 35:06.020
So stop going over and go home.

35:06.604 --> 35:09.315
I'll stay and hold down
the fort here, huh?

35:09.398 --> 35:11.067
[machine clicks, beeps]

35:16.114 --> 35:19.325
- Oh, hey, earlier--
- I'm sorry about before.

35:21.202 --> 35:23.538
[Si-woo] You were just asking
'cause you care about him,

35:23.621 --> 35:24.997
and I got defensive.

35:28.709 --> 35:30.253
You're right about me too.

35:30.336 --> 35:33.673
I keep acting like a child
when we talk about him.

35:34.257 --> 35:37.635
I try to stay rational, but it's so hard.

35:38.845 --> 35:40.721
[Si-woo] It's always been like that.

35:41.305 --> 35:43.015
My relationships start well.

35:44.517 --> 35:45.726
But my father…

35:46.936 --> 35:48.604
always ruins it.

35:51.357 --> 35:53.526
I just find him so tiring.

35:53.609 --> 35:58.322
It's my own father, and…
I didn't want to make the woman I love

35:58.406 --> 36:01.409
have to deal with him
as part of the family.

36:04.787 --> 36:06.038
Can't love be enough?

36:07.582 --> 36:10.168
Not everyone has to become family.

36:11.377 --> 36:15.798
The world keeps telling you
to take responsibility for your love,

36:16.841 --> 36:19.135
and that marriage is the only way
to do that.

36:19.760 --> 36:20.761
So…

36:23.181 --> 36:24.682
I told her we're over.

36:27.727 --> 36:29.729
[emotional music]

36:45.703 --> 36:46.829
[sighs]

36:49.540 --> 36:50.625
I'm sorry.

36:56.172 --> 36:59.091
It's okay. You don't have to apologize.

36:59.884 --> 37:00.885
I get it.

37:05.306 --> 37:08.559
[chuckles]
Really, I… I understand.

37:16.275 --> 37:17.151
Lee Si-woo.

37:19.195 --> 37:20.780
Why do you keep saying it's fine?

37:22.198 --> 37:25.868
Why do you keep telling me
that you understand why?

37:30.373 --> 37:33.459
What are you gonna do
if I try to get you back?

37:36.545 --> 37:38.089
If I beg and beg you,

37:39.006 --> 37:40.883
tell you that I just can't lose you…

37:51.477 --> 37:52.853
I still…

37:54.939 --> 37:56.816
like you a lot, Director.

37:59.902 --> 38:01.028
You know that?

38:09.620 --> 38:11.998
[Young-gil] Hey! Where is Director Jin?

38:12.581 --> 38:14.667
Director Jin! Hey!

38:20.006 --> 38:21.424
Hey, yo, Director!

38:22.049 --> 38:24.135
Director Jin Ha-kyung!

38:24.218 --> 38:25.219
Let's talk later.

38:28.472 --> 38:29.473
[door slides open]

38:29.557 --> 38:31.434
- [Young-gil] Where's Director Jin?
- [door closes]

38:32.226 --> 38:34.395
She screws up the entire forecast
and goes home already?

38:34.478 --> 38:36.355
Somebody go call your director!

38:37.398 --> 38:38.316
I'm here.

38:38.816 --> 38:43.279
You, who… Who said you
could redact a forecast, huh?

38:44.155 --> 38:46.407
The jet stream at 10 kilometers
is still strong.

38:46.991 --> 38:48.659
We don't believe it will clear.

38:48.743 --> 38:49.660
Hey.

38:50.411 --> 38:53.831
You think that Team One just adapts
your forecast like we're stupid?

38:53.914 --> 38:56.625
No, it's because we respect
the work the other team did.

38:56.709 --> 38:58.794
And we understand
the prior team's analysis

38:58.878 --> 39:01.047
is the most reliable source material.

39:01.130 --> 39:03.215
How dare you go and just throw
all our hard work away?

39:03.299 --> 39:05.801
It's not that I don't value
all your efforts.

39:05.885 --> 39:07.553
We revise predictions due to new evidence.

39:07.636 --> 39:09.680
And? What if you made a mistake?

39:09.764 --> 39:11.724
Who's gonna be responsible for this?

39:11.807 --> 39:13.976
Are you gonna take the fall
for the human lives at stake

39:14.060 --> 39:15.102
and the billions in costs?

39:15.186 --> 39:18.314
Are you saying when there's
an irregular pattern, I should do nothing

39:18.397 --> 39:21.275
just because someone more senior to me
is emotionally attached to their forecast?

39:21.359 --> 39:22.401
Huh?

39:25.112 --> 39:26.280
[chuckles]

39:27.073 --> 39:28.949
[phone vibrates]

39:29.033 --> 39:31.285
HEADQUARTERS
SHIN SEOK-HO

39:31.369 --> 39:32.828
Hmm, Mr. Shin here.

39:33.496 --> 39:35.373
Sir, where are you right now?
Are you near?

39:36.165 --> 39:39.251
Uh, I think you'll have
to come in again tonight.

39:39.335 --> 39:41.504
Why? What's going on?

39:41.587 --> 39:42.922
Director Choi from Chief Team One

39:43.005 --> 39:45.424
is raising hell here
about the redaction earlier.

39:45.508 --> 39:48.928
- What did you just say?
- [Seok-ho sighs]

39:49.011 --> 39:50.262
Say that one more time!

39:51.180 --> 39:53.891
- Say that one more time!
- Oh, no!

39:53.974 --> 39:56.519
- What do you think a director is, huh?
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

39:56.602 --> 39:58.854
- [Seok-ho] Director.
- Hey! What's going on?

39:58.938 --> 40:01.357
I gotta see my daughter now!

40:01.440 --> 40:04.944
It's her birthday! We're supposed
to eat out tonight! Come on!

40:05.027 --> 40:07.029
- …say to me?
- What are you doing, huh?

40:07.113 --> 40:09.407
- Who are you?
- We're talking.

40:09.490 --> 40:12.118
All that praise got to your head,
and now you're lost, huh?

40:12.201 --> 40:14.787
Apologize for what you just said
to me right now!

40:14.870 --> 40:15.996
Just say sorry!

40:17.581 --> 40:18.582
[scoffs]

40:18.666 --> 40:22.128
I won't. Everything I said
is exactly what I mean.

40:23.712 --> 40:25.923
Whoa!

40:26.006 --> 40:28.717
You turned into a real brat now, huh?

40:28.801 --> 40:30.511
- Stop--
- Who the hell are you?

40:30.594 --> 40:34.098
I'll show you how we handle
behavior like this around here.

40:34.181 --> 40:35.266
Now, what did you say to me?

40:35.349 --> 40:36.851
- Go on! Say it again, huh?
- Let go!

40:36.934 --> 40:38.978
- [Si-woo] Let go!
- Say it again!

40:39.061 --> 40:40.229
- I said let go of her!
- [thwacks]

40:40.312 --> 40:41.313
[grunts]

40:45.985 --> 40:49.238
[playful music]

40:49.989 --> 40:51.198
[body thuds]

40:53.742 --> 40:54.743
[groans]

41:00.791 --> 41:02.251
SENIOR FORECASTER UM DONG-HAN

41:02.334 --> 41:03.377
[Dong-han] Hello?

41:05.004 --> 41:06.172
What was that?

41:07.089 --> 41:08.132
Seok-ho.

41:10.426 --> 41:11.343
Seok-ho?

41:14.763 --> 41:16.015
[Young-gil moans]

41:17.475 --> 41:19.393
[sighs]
Si-woo.

41:22.563 --> 41:24.857
[breathing nervously]

41:27.485 --> 41:30.029
Oh, my goodness!
I can't believe it finally happened.

41:33.073 --> 41:33.949
[phone beeps]

41:34.533 --> 41:37.203
Yes, sir. This is Assistant Director Park.

41:37.286 --> 41:38.120
What?

41:43.417 --> 41:44.418
[moans]

41:46.837 --> 41:49.632
[groans]
For crying…

41:51.634 --> 41:52.801
[inhales deeply]

41:55.930 --> 41:58.724
[tires screech]

42:01.644 --> 42:04.146
[Bo-mi] I can't believe father
got a reservation here.

42:05.648 --> 42:07.733
You said you wanted to go somewhere nice.

42:08.400 --> 42:10.611
- This place is really trendy, Mom.
- Hmm.

42:10.694 --> 42:14.114
I was looking it up,
and tons of famous people come here.

42:14.198 --> 42:17.326
It's the hottest place
in Cheongdam-dong these days.

42:17.409 --> 42:19.119
I heard it's really hard to get into.

42:19.203 --> 42:22.373
Really? That's not like your pa.

42:22.456 --> 42:24.291
I guess he really made an effort.

42:24.375 --> 42:25.459
[chuckles]

42:27.002 --> 42:29.004
Uh, what should we get?

42:32.424 --> 42:34.093
[piano music playing]

42:34.176 --> 42:36.095
[phone vibrates]

42:36.178 --> 42:37.763
BO-MI'S DAD

42:43.269 --> 42:44.812
[exhales]

42:49.316 --> 42:51.068
Yes. What? Where are you right now?

42:51.652 --> 42:52.528
I…

42:53.153 --> 42:54.572
I was headed there.

42:55.155 --> 42:57.032
And, well… And I…

42:57.116 --> 42:59.868
[Dong-han] I just got a call
from the office. There's this…

42:59.952 --> 43:00.828
Forget it.

43:00.911 --> 43:02.162
Hyang-rae, I…

43:02.246 --> 43:03.789
- [Dong-han] I'll be there--
- I said fine.

43:04.373 --> 43:05.749
- [call ends]
- [sighs]

43:12.172 --> 43:14.341
What? Dad's not coming?

43:14.925 --> 43:15.801
[sighs]

43:17.928 --> 43:20.347
Yeah. You're dad had to…

43:22.057 --> 43:23.642
Today, of all days, hmm…

43:24.852 --> 43:27.396
- What should we do?
- Let's just eat by ourselves.

43:31.525 --> 43:33.485
Can I order the two things I want?

43:33.569 --> 43:35.321
I don't know when I'll come here again.

43:36.822 --> 43:39.158
[light music]

43:39.825 --> 43:42.244
[shutter clicking]

43:45.748 --> 43:48.208
[Young-gil] This is just
a habit to you, huh?

43:49.418 --> 43:51.378
It was just an accident, Director.

43:51.462 --> 43:54.548
[Seok-ho] He was trying to stop the fight.
It was an accident.

43:55.424 --> 43:57.551
You were the one who started it, Director.

43:57.635 --> 44:01.263
Forecaster Si-woo here
was trying to break it up, that's all.

44:01.764 --> 44:04.516
[scoffs]
Oh, right. Break it up, huh?

44:04.600 --> 44:07.811
Forecaster, this isn't your first time
assaulting someone, is it?

44:08.479 --> 44:11.732
I heard you punched
Han Ki-jun at the Spokesman's Office.

44:11.815 --> 44:13.817
If you wanna vent, take it out on me.

44:13.901 --> 44:15.986
Don't go harassing all of Team Two.

44:16.070 --> 44:17.404
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung.

44:17.488 --> 44:19.907
You should worry about the forecast,
not all these guys.

44:19.990 --> 44:22.451
What will you do when your forecast
is wrong after your redaction?

44:23.035 --> 44:25.829
What would you want, huh?
For me to resign?

44:26.747 --> 44:28.082
You just said it. You'll resign.

44:28.165 --> 44:29.958
Director, please just calm down.

44:30.042 --> 44:31.752
But if our forecast is correct,

44:31.835 --> 44:34.129
well, then, you should be
the one to resign, Director.

44:34.213 --> 44:36.298
- What?
- [Seok-ho] What is this, huh, Squid Game?

44:36.382 --> 44:37.883
One of you dies if you lose?

44:37.966 --> 44:40.761
Team One versus Team Two,
Director, and the loser resigns.

44:40.844 --> 44:44.223
We'll go down in KMA history books,
as an example of reckless leadership, huh?

44:44.306 --> 44:45.391
How about it? Let's go.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.059
You snarky little…

44:47.142 --> 44:48.477
[Dong-han] Stop it! Stop!

44:48.560 --> 44:51.063
Give it a rest, people, huh?

44:51.146 --> 44:54.024
What are you fighting about?
Is your nose bleeding?

44:55.401 --> 44:56.860
[sighs]

44:57.444 --> 44:58.654
What are you doing?

44:59.238 --> 45:03.117
Why? What are you people doing here
just fighting over weather?

45:04.284 --> 45:05.369
I didn't hit anyone.

45:05.953 --> 45:07.913
Uh, I… hit him.

45:08.497 --> 45:09.790
[Myung-ju] It was an accident.

45:09.873 --> 45:11.750
No, really, it was.

45:12.459 --> 45:14.628
[sighs]
They came at me three to one.

45:15.254 --> 45:18.715
I wanna make this clear.
I was trying to stop the fight.

45:20.050 --> 45:22.636
[Young-gil] Never mind that.
Senior Forecaster Um.

45:22.719 --> 45:24.805
How do you train all these guys?
They're a mess!

45:24.888 --> 45:26.432
I told you that weather is a fluid thing,

45:26.515 --> 45:29.435
not something you can reverse
with a few numbers. I told you that!

45:29.518 --> 45:32.563
And then, you all have
to run and go throw away

45:32.646 --> 45:36.233
weeks of analysis just because
there's a couple ensemble scenarios

45:36.316 --> 45:37.568
that look odd?

45:37.651 --> 45:38.986
What?

45:39.069 --> 45:41.738
You redacted my forecast before too.

45:42.239 --> 45:44.116
- I did?
- You did?

45:44.199 --> 45:45.159
Two times, yeah.

45:46.410 --> 45:47.744
Really? Twice?

45:48.954 --> 45:50.164
And when did I do that?

45:50.247 --> 45:54.376
2004, summer heat wave.
2011 fall, the cold air.

45:54.460 --> 45:56.044
You got one right, and I got one right.

45:56.128 --> 45:57.754
But I… I never scolded you

45:57.838 --> 46:00.048
about the times that you went
and messed with it.

46:00.132 --> 46:01.467
Because I…

46:01.550 --> 46:05.179
I had faith in you, absolute!
And I thought you were sure.

46:05.262 --> 46:09.224
But you're… you're a senior!
You should have the same faith in her! No?

46:09.808 --> 46:13.145
Instead you come here
and make a mess 'cause of one revision?

46:13.228 --> 46:17.441
'Cause she's a little snot.
We can't talk if she won't listen to us!

46:17.524 --> 46:18.567
[Dong-han] Director Choi.

46:19.485 --> 46:21.153
She's Team Two's director.

46:22.488 --> 46:24.198
She's the same rank as you.

46:24.281 --> 46:27.743
Director Jin has the same responsibility
and authority as you.

46:28.744 --> 46:31.371
How are you gonna come in here
and push her around with age?

46:31.455 --> 46:33.999
It's not the '80s, man! "Snot"?

46:34.082 --> 46:35.501
Is our director a child?

46:40.631 --> 46:42.799
So I got a little angry, huh? So what?

46:42.883 --> 46:45.219
Yeah, you got that angry
over a weather issue.

46:45.302 --> 46:47.846
Trust me, no one's as angry
as I am here, okay?

46:47.930 --> 46:50.015
It's my daughter's birthday dinner now!

46:50.098 --> 46:52.643
I was going to have
a normal meal out with her

46:52.726 --> 46:55.145
for the first real time in ten years.

46:55.229 --> 46:56.563
I even did my hair.

46:56.647 --> 47:00.817
I was gonna be a real dad for once,
and now they're probably already done!

47:00.901 --> 47:02.152
[tongue clicks]

47:08.408 --> 47:11.078
Excuse me. The difference
in atmospheric pressure

47:11.161 --> 47:12.913
around Siberia is dropping.

47:15.332 --> 47:18.168
- [Young-gil] What the…
- [monitor trills]

47:18.794 --> 47:19.628
Ms. Lee.

47:19.711 --> 47:23.090
Track back the hourly development
situation in the global model.

47:23.674 --> 47:24.591
Hmm.

47:28.762 --> 47:30.430
[Ms. Lee] The jet stream is moving south.

47:31.181 --> 47:32.266
[Young-gil] The… the…

47:33.100 --> 47:36.061
The… Well, it shouldn't be falling.

47:41.275 --> 47:42.693
Go home. Your shift's over.

47:44.736 --> 47:45.571
Go home.

47:46.154 --> 47:48.156
[upbeat music]

47:49.950 --> 47:51.118
[Young-gil] Damn it!

48:08.760 --> 48:10.178
[soft laughter]

48:18.353 --> 48:20.564
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.692
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:30.741 --> 48:32.075
[automated voice] Door is closing.

48:40.709 --> 48:41.793
Oppa.

48:44.087 --> 48:46.465
It's late. You're still working?

48:47.257 --> 48:48.175
Mm.

48:48.675 --> 48:50.844
I'm just not feeling too great.

48:56.975 --> 48:59.686
I was worried. You looked white
as a sheet in the press room.

49:01.730 --> 49:03.190
Does it hurt anywhere else?

49:03.857 --> 49:05.525
Mm, no, I'm okay.

49:08.612 --> 49:11.865
[Ki-jun sighs]
I've been thinking, Yu-jin.

49:13.742 --> 49:14.993
The kid…

49:17.204 --> 49:18.121
I'm grateful for it.

49:20.290 --> 49:22.125
[emotional music]

49:24.211 --> 49:25.379
I know…

49:26.463 --> 49:28.173
I'm not ready as a father right now.

49:30.425 --> 49:33.845
And when it comes,
there'll be moments when I flounder

49:34.429 --> 49:35.847
and lose my cool.

49:35.931 --> 49:38.642
And I know I'll look like
such a fool when it happens.

49:40.185 --> 49:41.895
It's our kid, though.

49:43.105 --> 49:44.815
And I wanna do my very best.

49:44.898 --> 49:47.526
[breathes deeply]

49:47.609 --> 49:49.861
- Oppa, I--
- [Ki-jun] But…

49:50.529 --> 49:53.448
even if I feel that way,
if you're not sure, Yu-jin,

49:55.117 --> 49:56.368
I'll honor your choices.

49:58.870 --> 50:01.373
I don't wanna force that sacrifice on you.

50:06.253 --> 50:12.843
All I can tell you now is that really,
no matter what you decide,

50:14.094 --> 50:15.554
I will be there for you.

50:16.638 --> 50:20.142
I'm gonna be right there the whole time,

50:21.935 --> 50:23.103
so you won't be alone.

50:23.937 --> 50:26.189
[soft emotional music]

50:33.155 --> 50:34.906
[chuckles]
I'm hungry.

50:35.532 --> 50:36.491
Wanna go eat?

51:09.983 --> 51:11.485
[sighs]

51:35.217 --> 51:36.051
[sighs]

51:53.360 --> 51:54.945
[Seok-ho] Whoa! All this?

51:55.737 --> 51:59.157
I have the ingredients
so I thought I would, you know.

51:59.241 --> 52:00.700
Well, it smells great.

52:01.284 --> 52:03.286
My mom and I are both great cooks.

52:03.870 --> 52:04.746
Wow!

52:15.215 --> 52:16.091
[Seok-ho] Whoa!

52:16.758 --> 52:17.926
Is there anything that…

52:18.677 --> 52:20.720
that you're not great at, huh?

52:21.471 --> 52:24.015
You're a great artist,
great cook, great charisma.

52:24.099 --> 52:26.142
[giggles]
You think?

52:28.436 --> 52:30.647
You're great at, well, everything
except writing stories.

52:38.363 --> 52:40.031
What about my stories?

52:40.115 --> 52:42.075
What don't you like about them?

52:42.158 --> 52:44.995
Mm-mm. No, it's just that…

52:45.579 --> 52:46.663
They're not bad.

52:46.746 --> 52:50.333
They don't have a hook,
something that hooks you in.

52:51.710 --> 52:55.088
Oh, a hook, okay.

52:55.171 --> 52:59.467
Yeah. But your artwork's
still super cute, right?

53:01.344 --> 53:02.637
[Seok-ho] Mmm…

53:06.391 --> 53:08.226
[tense music]

53:08.310 --> 53:10.186
So what you're saying
is my stories are bad

53:10.270 --> 53:12.355
because they don't have a hook, right?

53:13.148 --> 53:17.235
No. Uh, well, I never said bad, really.

53:17.319 --> 53:19.237
And that my writing doesn't sell.

53:19.821 --> 53:21.323
I don't think I said that.

53:21.406 --> 53:25.368
You were suggesting it when you said
that the hooks in my stories were lacking.

53:31.625 --> 53:34.336
- Well… wine? Want it?
- [utensil clanks]

53:34.419 --> 53:37.047
- Here. You want some, hmm?
- No.

53:38.340 --> 53:39.758
I wanna talk about my writing.

53:45.096 --> 53:47.766
[tense music]

53:47.849 --> 53:50.018
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

53:53.855 --> 53:55.482
- Door is closing.
- [sighs]

53:56.983 --> 53:59.527
[door lock beeping]

54:01.404 --> 54:02.822
[error tone]

54:03.365 --> 54:04.199
[Mrs. Bae] Huh?

54:05.867 --> 54:08.620
[keypad beeping]

54:10.080 --> 54:11.665
[error tone]

54:14.668 --> 54:17.212
Did she change the password
for her front door?

54:25.720 --> 54:29.391
[line ringing]

54:29.474 --> 54:31.267
Did you change your password?

54:31.851 --> 54:35.146
Yes, recently. I deserve my privacy.

54:35.230 --> 54:38.191
Enough of that!
Now what is the new combination?

54:39.317 --> 54:41.194
I'm sorry, Mom. I'll see you later.

54:46.616 --> 54:47.993
You could have told her.

54:48.493 --> 54:49.619
[Si-woo] It's cold out.

54:50.954 --> 54:53.206
It's okay. She's stronger than you think.

55:01.172 --> 55:04.384
So where are we going right now?

55:07.178 --> 55:08.054
The doctor.

55:10.515 --> 55:12.350
Heartless little wench.

55:13.560 --> 55:16.563
How can this girl of mine
be so cold-hearted?

55:17.439 --> 55:18.565
[sighs]

55:19.357 --> 55:22.986
What should I do?
I can't just take all of these back now.

55:27.490 --> 55:30.994
[apron rustles]

55:32.871 --> 55:33.913
Tell me!

55:33.997 --> 55:37.417
Tell me what you don't like
about my stories and be specific.

55:38.168 --> 55:41.588
It's… not that I don't like them. It's…

55:42.547 --> 55:44.674
Why do you keep saying
opposite things, huh?

55:44.758 --> 55:48.428
I'm serious! You said there
wasn't a hook, so explain, huh?

55:48.511 --> 55:50.472
Oh, the hook. It's, um…

55:51.473 --> 55:54.726
You're a lot more, uh, persistent
than I thought you would be.

55:55.477 --> 55:58.772
You can't be a writer if you're not
a persistent person, you know.

55:58.855 --> 56:01.733
For all those hours and days
you draw, and write and rewrite,

56:01.816 --> 56:03.818
and edit, and slave over your art.

56:03.902 --> 56:06.905
Have you ever laid awake all night
because you couldn't think

56:06.988 --> 56:08.948
of this one word you were looking for?

56:09.741 --> 56:11.910
I spend a week agonizing over one line,

56:11.993 --> 56:14.037
until my head feels
like it's gonna explode!

56:14.120 --> 56:17.165
I keep writing and rewriting
for what feels like forever!

56:17.248 --> 56:21.211
Every noun, every last article,
I write and rewrite 10,000 times,

56:21.294 --> 56:23.755
hoping I can make
even one sentence more dynamic,

56:23.838 --> 56:27.967
hoping I can better express myself
and just hoping it will work for someone.

56:28.802 --> 56:29.886
I'm sorry.

56:30.470 --> 56:32.847
And I know you can just look
at the final product,

56:32.931 --> 56:34.933
and say, "Oh, it's bad or it needs work."

56:35.016 --> 56:37.602
But don't be so quick to judge
my work and just ignore

56:37.685 --> 56:39.312
all the effort that it takes.

56:40.480 --> 56:42.273
I never did that.

56:43.233 --> 56:47.529
I'm an unpopular author
who can't sell a copy.

56:47.612 --> 56:49.405
But I have my pride still.

56:50.073 --> 56:53.284
I pride myself in knowing
that at least my writing

56:53.827 --> 56:56.913
and illustrations are gonna help
some children

56:56.996 --> 56:59.791
have a little more sunshine
in their lives, okay?

57:00.834 --> 57:02.710
Of course. I'll keep that in mind.

57:03.419 --> 57:04.838
All right, then.

57:07.340 --> 57:09.384
[sighs]
Don't go.

57:11.970 --> 57:13.012
Tae-kyung.

57:14.347 --> 57:15.348
Tae-kyung.

57:17.058 --> 57:18.309
You can't just go.

57:19.060 --> 57:20.770
What do you want me to do?

57:20.854 --> 57:22.063
[sighs]

57:23.481 --> 57:24.774
I'm really…

57:26.317 --> 57:27.819
really sorry about it.

57:29.320 --> 57:30.447
Don't leave, okay?

57:31.865 --> 57:32.907
[exhales]

57:35.827 --> 57:38.538
[thumping and moaning]

57:40.331 --> 57:43.334
[playful music]

57:48.131 --> 57:49.257
[Tae-kyung giggles]

57:51.342 --> 57:53.470
Oh, dear. Oh, dear. What do I do?

57:58.099 --> 57:59.184
- [doorknob clanks]
- [moans]

58:01.728 --> 58:03.563
- Ooh!
- Whoa!

58:04.772 --> 58:06.649
- [Tae-kyung] Are you okay?
- [Mrs. Bae mumbling]

58:06.733 --> 58:08.651
- Are you good? Are you good?
- Oh, my god.

58:08.735 --> 58:10.236
- [Seok-ho] Are you all right?
- Oh, dear!

58:11.779 --> 58:13.990
[both giggling]

58:18.411 --> 58:19.454
Tae… Tae-kyung.

58:20.038 --> 58:21.039
Yes?

58:21.748 --> 58:23.541
[suspenseful music]

58:26.961 --> 58:28.046
[gasps]

58:28.129 --> 58:31.633
Oh! Uh… Uh…

58:32.258 --> 58:35.011
- What? What?
- Huh?

58:36.221 --> 58:37.430
[Mrs. Bae] You!

58:38.014 --> 58:40.016
- Jin Tae-kyung!
- [Tae-kyung shouts]

58:40.099 --> 58:42.894
- [Tae-kyung] Mom! Mom!
- [Seok-ho] Please calm down, ma'am!

58:42.977 --> 58:45.647
CHAYOUNG HOSPITAL

58:52.695 --> 58:53.905
Is somebody sick?

58:55.156 --> 58:56.282
Room 309.

58:57.408 --> 58:59.536
The attending physician's on call today.

59:01.246 --> 59:02.872
So you can go in and…

59:32.485 --> 59:34.821
[machine beeping]

59:39.742 --> 59:42.370
LEE MYUNG-HAN

59:48.293 --> 59:51.212
[machine beeping]

59:55.425 --> 59:58.386
[breathes deeply]

01:00:18.323 --> 01:00:20.700
[emotional music]

01:00:20.783 --> 01:00:24.078
We have the PET CT results
and the sputum results as well.

01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:27.915
And, well, it's… it's cancer.

01:00:27.999 --> 01:00:30.543
It's already advanced to stage three.

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:36.174
If you take a look
at the PET CT scan here,

01:00:37.425 --> 01:00:40.595
it's metastasized
above the lymph nodes on the right.

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:47.393
[doctor] He must have been
in a great deal of pain.

01:01:01.616 --> 01:01:03.201
[sobbing]

01:01:06.954 --> 01:01:08.039
Father.

01:01:24.263 --> 01:01:26.140
Why would you do this to me?

01:01:28.226 --> 01:01:29.268
Why?

01:01:32.397 --> 01:01:33.439
Why?

01:01:35.233 --> 01:01:36.984
Why are you doing this?

01:01:38.277 --> 01:01:40.613
[sobbing]

01:01:59.006 --> 01:02:01.634
[sobbing]

01:02:10.268 --> 01:02:11.227
Excuse me.

01:02:12.145 --> 01:02:14.230
Is a Mr. Lee Myung-han here?

01:02:14.814 --> 01:02:16.649
[cop] They brought him in for a car crash.

01:02:16.733 --> 01:02:17.859
What do you need?

01:02:19.861 --> 01:02:21.028
[Yu-jin groans]

01:02:27.160 --> 01:02:28.286
[moans]

01:02:28.911 --> 01:02:30.788
- Oppa.
- Hmm?

01:02:31.998 --> 01:02:34.208
- Help me.
- What is it?

01:02:36.294 --> 01:02:38.796
- My stomach.
- Huh?

01:02:42.008 --> 01:02:43.676
Yu-jin, what's… what's wrong?
Where does it hurt?

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:45.511
My stomach hurts so much.

01:02:46.095 --> 01:02:48.473
Hey, Yu-jin, what's wrong, huh?
Hey, Yu-jin, huh?

01:02:49.348 --> 01:02:50.725
[exhales]

01:02:53.060 --> 01:02:55.813
[Si-woo] The rain said to the wind…

01:02:59.358 --> 01:03:00.985
What's your relationship
with Lee Myung-han?

01:03:03.070 --> 01:03:04.363
Well, his guardian.

01:03:05.740 --> 01:03:06.949
We're the police.

01:03:07.700 --> 01:03:10.244
There's an arrest warrant out
for Mr. Lee Myung-han.

01:03:10.328 --> 01:03:12.830
Charges are extortion and insurance fraud.

01:03:12.914 --> 01:03:14.916
[suspenseful music]

01:03:37.647 --> 01:03:38.898
[Si-woo] "You roar."

01:03:41.734 --> 01:03:43.361
"And I'll fall."

01:03:45.655 --> 01:03:48.616
["Open Your Heart" by Lyn playing]

01:04:12.306 --> 01:04:15.059
[Bong-chan] I found out
that getting something wrong

01:04:15.142 --> 01:04:17.603
can often teach you
more than getting something right.

01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:19.689
[Mrs. Bae] Do you know what the most
ridiculous thing in the world

01:04:19.772 --> 01:04:20.898
you can say is?

01:04:21.482 --> 01:04:23.359
That you're breaking up out of love.

01:04:24.610 --> 01:04:25.903
[Ki-jun] Don't let Lee Si-woo go.

01:04:25.987 --> 01:04:28.573
Not for Lee Si-woo, but for yourself.

01:04:30.032 --> 01:04:32.201
[Si-woo] Because it's you, Jin Ha-kyung.

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:36.914
[Ha-kyung] Because it's you, Lee Si-woo.

01:04:39.166 --> 01:04:41.419
[Si-woo] Because I just like you.

01:04:42.545 --> 01:04:44.255
[Ha-kyung] Because I like being with you.
